# Shell scripts run under bash on every platform, which a CRLF checkout breaks.
*.sh text eol=lf

# THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES is cargo-about output, and CI fails unless a fresh generation matches it byte
# for byte. Some dependencies ship their licence with CRLF line endings and cargo-about copies them
# verbatim, so git must store the file exactly as generated and never convert its line endings.
THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES -text
# The template must render the same on every platform, so it is never checked out with CRLF.
about.hbs text eol=lf
